.png | State is a dropdown |\n\nThis page documents the checkout delivery address form field structure per country across the four domestic storefronts (AU, EU, UK, US). All storefronts share a consistent base field set. The State/Region field appears across all storefronts but is labelled differently depending on the storefront — \"State\" for AU and US, and \"County/Region\" for EU and UK. It also renders as either a dropdown or free text field depending on the country selected. The mobile country prefix is pre-selected based on the active country in all cases.\n\n**Base fields — consistent across all storefronts:**  \nFirst Name, Last Name, Country, Address 1, Address 2, City/Suburb, State/County/Region (label varies per storefront), Postcode, Mobile Prefix (pre-selected), Mobile.\n\n**AU Storefront (21 countries):** Australia is the only country with a State dropdown. All other Oceania countries (NZ, Fiji, American Samoa, Cook Islands, Guam, Kiribati, Marshall Islands, Micronesia, Nauru, New Caledonia, Niue, Northern Mariana Islands, Palau, Papua New Guinea, Samoa, Solomon Islands, Tonga, Tuvalu, Vanuatu) use a free text State field.\n\n**EU Storefront (29 countries):** 19 countries use a County/Region dropdown (Austria, Belgium, Bulgaria, Croatia, Czechia, Denmark, Estonia, Finland, France, Germany, Greece, Italy, Latvia, Lithuania, Poland, Portugal, Romania, Spain, Sweden). 11 countries use a free text County/Region field (Andorra, Cyprus, Hungary, Ireland, Luxembourg, Malta, Monaco, Netherlands, San Marino, Slovakia, Slovenia).\n\n**UK Storefront (1 country):** No variation — County/Region is always a free text field.\n\n**US Storefront (2 countries):** United States uses a State dropdown. Puerto Rico is a unique edge case — State is pre-filled with \"PR\" and disabled, as it is a US territory with a fixed state code.\n\n**Note:** Postcode format validation per country is a separate concern documented in SFCC-675.\n\nTo confirm; can the country be changed, can the mobile pre-fix be changed?"
